<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shaushtatar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1450 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century-bce">15th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shaushtatar was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a> around 1450 BCE, under whom the kingdom reached a peak of power. Accounts of the Mitanni Empire describe him as ruling a centralised polity capable of projecting military force. He campaigned against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a> and asserted authority over subordinate states.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>By the reign of <b>Shaushtatar</b> (c. 1450 BCE), Mitanni was a powerful kingdom able to project military force, as shown by his sack of Ashur and his authority over vassals such as Arrapha, whose archives survive at Nuzi.</blockquote><a href="/empire/mitanni-empire">Mitanni Empire · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
